C. Snow accents

Add subtle winter snow details around selected:

- Buttons.
- Cards.
- Sidebar elements.
- Section headers.
- Seasonal widgets.
- Important dashboard elements.

Snow should appear as a visual accent, not a thick overlay.

Do not add unnecessary borders or decorative outlines.

D. Candy-cane decorations

Add the recognizable red-and-white striped winter sticks (candy-cane style).

Use them selectively:

- Seasonal dashboard decorations.
- Santa gift presentation.
- Winter Festival banners.
- Selected section accents.

Do not place them beside every component.

E. Winter cookies

Introduce cute, visually polished winter cookies.

They may appear as:

- Small decorative illustrations.
- Seasonal dashboard accents.
- Santa gift visuals.
- Winter task rewards.
- Seasonal collectibles.

Create original visuals or use the existing icon/illustration system.

Do not depend on unnecessary external image downloads.

F. Theme consistency

Ensure the Winter Theme works across:

- Student Dashboard.
- Faculty Dashboard.
- Study Dashboard.
- Sidebar.
- Relevant navigation elements.
- Cards and widgets.
- Buttons.
- Dialogs.
- Notification center.
- Gamification areas.
- Responsive layouts.

Avoid changing unrelated module functionality.

G. Theme control

The Winter Theme must be controlled by the Super Admin Feature & Theme Management system.

When enabled:

- Eligible users receive the Winter Theme.
