7. WINTER SPIN WHEEL — TWO-HOUR COOLDOWN

Introduce a separate Spin Wheel gamification system.

This is a recurring, lightweight reward activity.

It is not as special as the nightly Santa gift.

A. Availability

The Spin Wheel becomes available again every two hours after a successful claim.

Requirements:

- A server-authoritative cooldown.
- Persistent last-claim timestamp.
- A per-user cooldown record.
- Accurate remaining-time display.
- No bypass through refreshing.
- No bypass through changing device time.
- No duplicate reward claims.

The next eligible time must be calculated by the backend.

B. Spin Wheel interface

Create a polished, visually attractive wheel.

Possible segments:

- Small XP reward.
- Moderate XP reward.
- Small streak-related bonus.
- Small AI quota bonus.
- Winter cookie collectible.
- Seasonal badge progress.
- Surprise common reward.
- No additional reward, if clearly disclosed and appropriate.

The wheel should have a balanced, transparent reward pool.

Display the reward probabilities before the user spins.

Do not create misleading odds or imply that a specific outcome is guaranteed.

C. Wheel animations

Implement:

- Wheel rotation.
- Smooth acceleration.
- Gradual deceleration.
- Accurate stopping on the server-selected result.
- Reward reveal.
- Subtle celebration effects.
- Accessible result announcement.

The wheel must stop at the actual server-selected reward.

Do not let the frontend select a reward independently from the backend.

D. Sound effects

Add optional sound effects:

- Spin start.
- Rotation ticks where appropriate.
- Wheel stop.
- Reward reveal.

Requirements:

- Respect device and browser autoplay restrictions.
- Do not play sound without a valid user interaction.
- Provide a mute option.
- Respect existing sound preferences if available.
- Avoid excessive or repetitive sounds.
- Provide a silent experience by default if the application has no established sound preference.

E. Floating wheel icon and toast

When the wheel becomes available:

- Display a small, attractive toast informing the user.
- Show a floating wheel icon.
- Make the icon clickable.
- Open the wheel interface when clicked.

After a user successfully spins:

- Keep the wheel icon visible.
- Reduce its visual prominence and opacity.
- Do not keep showing availability notifications.
- When the user clicks it, show the remaining cooldown time.
- Display the next eligible time clearly.

When the cooldown expires:

- Restore its available appearance.
- Show an appropriate toast.
- Make the wheel available again.

Avoid repeatedly showing toasts on every render or page navigation.

Use a persistent notification state or appropriate event tracking so the same availability notification is not spammed.

F. Wheel reward history

Store:

- User ID.
- Spin timestamp.
- Selected reward.
- Reward amount or identifier.
- Reward application status.
- Associated event ID.

Allow users to view a small reward history.

