8. REWARD ENGINE — CENTRALIZED AND SECURE

Do not implement independent random reward logic in multiple components.

Build a centralized reward engine.

It should support:

- Santa gifts.
- Spin Wheel rewards.
- Winter task rewards.
- Badge rewards.
- XP rewards.
- AI quota rewards.
- Seasonal collectibles.
- Future gamification rewards.

Backend requirements

All random reward selection and reward application must be server-side.

Use secure random selection appropriate to the reward mechanism.

Implement:

- Reward definitions.
- Rarity configuration.
- Reward probabilities.
- Eligibility checks.
- Claim cooldowns.
- Duplicate prevention.
- Atomic reward claims.
- Reward transaction history.
- Idempotency.
- Reward application status.
- Administrative auditability.

Do not trust client-provided reward names, amounts, rarity, XP, or cooldown timestamps.

A user must not be able to modify a frontend request to grant themselves more XP or AI quota.

Use database constraints and transactions or equivalent reliable server-side atomic operations.

If an existing XP or reward service exists, extend it instead of creating a duplicate.

Responsible gamification

This is a student platform.

Keep the reward systems fun, optional, and age-appropriate.

- No purchases or paid spins.
- No premium currency gambling.
- No cash-equivalent rewards.
- No pressure to claim rewards.
- No punishment for missing a reward.
- No manipulative scarcity messages.
- No misleading odds.
- No unnecessary interruptions.
- No reward mechanics that interfere with studying.

Make the experience celebratory, not addictive.

